    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that it's \"complex\" but that kinda feels like an avoidant answer lol. if you look at the actual track record, they seem to fail way more often than they work. like, if they usually just hurt regular people instead of changing anything, isn't it more accurate to say they're just a form of bullying disguised as policy?",
